1Ki 2:1 , David, having given a charge to Solomon
1Ki 2:3 , of religiousness;
1Ki 2:5 , of Joab;
1Ki 2:7 , of Barzillai;
1Ki 2:8 , of Shimei;
1Ki 2:10 , dies;
1Ki 2:12 , Solomon succeeds;
1Ki 2:13 , Adonijah, moving Bath-sheba to sue unto Solomon for Abishag, is put to death;
1Ki 2:26 , Abiathar, having his life given him, is deprived of the priesthood;
1Ki 2:28 , Joab fleeing to the horns of the altar, is there slain;
1Ki 2:35 , Benaiah is put in Joab's room, and Zadok in Abiathar's;
1Ki 2:36 , Shimei, confined to Jerusalem, by occasion of going thence to Gath, is put to death.
